 "title": "Describing material properties",
 "audience": "family",
 "keyIdea": "We describe materials with pairs of words: hard or soft, stiff or bendy, shiny or dull, waterproof or not.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "Is it hard or soft? Is it shiny or dull? Does it bend? Does water soak in?",
   "These words tell us what a material is like."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "Property words come in opposite pairs: hard/soft, stiff/bendy (flexible), shiny/dull, rough/smooth, waterproof/absorbent, transparent/opaque. Testing is better than guessing.",
   "Let children test: bend it, drip water on it, scratch it with a coin, shine a torch at it. Then name the property in a sentence: 'foil is shiny and bendy'."
  ]
 },
